# TEMPLATE: .npmrc (repo root)
# WHAT: supply-chain age policy. Refuse to resolve a dependency version younger than 14 days.
# CHANGE: nothing. Keep in step with `cooldown:` in .github/dependabot.yml (check-release fails if either disappears).
# GUARDS: a malicious npm release is usually live for hours to days before it is pulled. Applies to `npm install`,
#         `npm update`, `npm audit fix`; `npm ci` is NOT affected (it installs exactly what package-lock.json pins), so
#         Dependabot's cooldown is the matching control for what lands in the lockfile. Needs npm >= 11.10 (older npm
#         ignores the key silently; check-release also verifies the npm version).
#
# Deliberate exception for an urgent NON-security fix: add the package to `min-release-age-exclude[]=<name>` below, in
# the same PR, so it is visible in review and revertible. Never pass --min-release-age=0 in a commit or workflow.
min-release-age=14
